Turn off the graph subsystem: we only need xport, and rrd_graph pulls in
Cairo, Pango, gobject and libpng.  Together with
0006-xport-without-graph.dif this drops those four dependencies while
keeping rrdtool xport and rrdtool.xport() from the Python binding.

Note that src/rrd_config.h is a *generated* file shipped inside the
release tarball; if the tarball is ever refreshed, re-check this hunk.

diff --git a/src/rrd_config.h b/src/rrd_config.h
--- a/src/rrd_config.h
+++ b/src/rrd_config.h
@@ -280,8 +280,8 @@
 /* Define to 1 if you have the `readdir' function. */
 #define HAVE_READDIR 1
 
-/* is rrd_graph supported by this install */
-#define HAVE_RRD_GRAPH /**/
+/* is rrd_graph supported by this install -- disabled, see
+   0006-xport-without-graph.dif */
 
 /* is rrd_restore supported by this install */
 #define HAVE_RRD_RESTORE /**/
